=== ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS ===
  • Data seam: own protocol `FeatureFlagChangesSource` + `InMemoryFeatureFlagChangesSource` (NO `import Shared`) so the
    surface host-compiles WITHOUT the unstaged KMP xcframework. The web `ChangesPanel` is presentational (props
    `rows`/`loading`/`scopedKey`); the native surface elevates those props into the P1/S8 cache-then-network state
    holder (the flag-change feed) and the view performs ZERO HTTP. A `ChangesPanelModel(rows:loading:scopedKey:)`
    web-prop initializer preserves the exact `<ChangesPanel rows loading scopedKey/>` call site.
  • Load state: self-contained `ChangesPanelLoadState` + `ChangesPanelError` mirroring the facade `LoadableState`/
    `FacadeError` SHAPE (cached-behind-refresh, ADR-013 stale, offline-keeps-cache, retryable) — so the production
    binding is a 1:1 map and every branch is unit-testable. The web shell only branches on loading/`rows.length`;
    the resolver is a documented SUPERSET adding the prompt's stale/offline/error chrome.
  • Value preview (the surface-specific parity point): the web source defines an inline `compact(value)` that
    `JSON.stringify`s the arbitrary `old_value`/`new_value` (`FeatureFlagValue = unknown`) and clamps to 60 chars
    (`s.slice(0,57)+'…'`). Reproduced exactly by `FlagValue` (recursive JSON value) + `compactJSON` (JS number
    formatting — integral values drop the decimal, matching that JS parses every JSON number as Double; JS string
    escaping — forward slashes NOT escaped; sorted object keys — matching the Go `encoding/json` sorted-key wire).
    CRITICAL decode decision: the row DTO uses EXPLICIT CodingKeys, NOT `.convertFromSnakeCase`, because a global
    snake→camel strategy also rewrites the NESTED object keys inside old_value/new_value and would corrupt the
    preview (`{"feature_x":true}` → `{"featureX":true}`). A dedicated test pins this.
  • Operation token: the web Badge renders `{row.operation}` VERBATIM (a stable server data value, NOT a `t()` call),
    so the native chip renders the raw token verbatim and the OP_VARIANT map (set→success, delete→danger, else
    neutral) drives only the tone. No i18n key is invented for `set`/`delete` — faithful to the source.
  • i18n: per-surface `.strings` table + `ChangesPanelStrings` facade (NSLocalizedString tableName + value fallback) —
    parallel-safe across the concurrent slots; the shared Localizable.xcstrings is NOT edited (Honesty rule 7). The
    scoped empty message keeps the web i18next `{{key}}` token and interpolates it at the render edge.
  • Table: hand-composed (not the shared `TSDataTable`) because TSDataTable takes main-catalog `LocalizedStringKey`
    headers (no per-surface fallback) and always renders a selection column the read-only audit log has not — the
    same disposition the 0026 AuditPanel + 0069 NotificationStatsWidget logs record. The shared `TSTone` (op chip
    color) and `TSSkeleton` (loading) ARE reused; the empty state is the shared `ContentUnavailableView` pattern
    with facade `Text` (web `EmptyState`).
  • Telemetry: REUSES the canonical `DashboardWidgetTelemetryEvent` / `DashboardWidgetTelemetrySink` /
    `BufferedDashboardWidgetTelemetry` (Sources/DashboardWidgets/BatteryCellsWidgetRegistry.swift), the app-wide
    P1/S11 diagnostics seam. `ChangesPanel.viewOpenedEvent == .viewOpened(surface:"ChangesPanel")`, emitted on `.task`.
  • Proto/units note: flag operations + values are opaque config data; no unit-suffixed fields are involved, so the
    Phase-48 SI-canonical rules do not apply to this surface.

